# L §5.16: "A random fact is an input or def of type dist U"; Closed forms: "mean(e), e a sum of known multiples of
# random facts plus a known constant: the same sum of their means"; normal(m, s) has mean m. g (a def) and g2 (an
# input) are random facts with mean 10 PLN (writer 5's T-74, stated; `mean` of a distribution value written inline,
# `mean(normal(mu, sd))`, is refused LOAD-RANDOM since round 18, C1-47, L5_16_mean_of_dist_value).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input mu: money PLN
input sd: money PLN
input g2: dist PLN
def g: dist PLN = normal(mu, sd) to 0.01 PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  mu = 10.00 PLN
  sd = 2.00 PLN
  g2 = normal(10 PLN, 2 PLN) to 0.01 PLN

ask q: mean(g)
ask q2: mean(g2)
=== expect
q: 10 PLN (horizon none)
  cut 2026-10-18
q2: 10 PLN (horizon none)
  cut 2026-10-18
